<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lahore</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lahore is a major city in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a>, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a>, with a long history as a centre of political power. It was the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a> from 1799, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranjit-singh">Ranjit Singh</a> took it, and the seat of the Lahore Darbar. Earlier, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nader-shah">Nader Shah</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afsharid-empire">Afsharid Empire</a> passed through Lahore on his invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lahore.jpg" alt="Lahore" width="320" height="234" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rohaan Bhatti · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lahore_Fort_view_from_Baradari.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
